DASH.todo={title:"What to do as a normal investor",note:"General info, not personal financial advice.",
l:["<b>Don't panic-sell a correction.</b> The S&P is now 10%+ below its record after an 8.6% week. Corrections are normal, and only about a third of those since 1983 became bear markets; selling after the drop locks in losses.",
"<b>Keep investing regularly, not all at once.</b> Fear & Greed hit 10 and NYSE new lows (565) crushed new highs (14). Fixed monthly buys (DCA) beat guessing the bottom, which nobody can call.",
"<b>Check your AI and chip exposure.</b> Nvidia fell 14% in a day and AMD and Micron ~13-14%. If one theme has grown into a big share of your money, trim back to your plan; a broad index fund already holds the big AI names.",
"<b>Cash and short bonds earn while you wait.</b> 2-year Treasuries pay ~4.6-4.7% and a Fed hike is still ~92% likely. Keep your emergency fund and near-term money there, not in stocks.",
"<b>Don't chase a hot IPO.</b> Anthropic rose 17% on day one, then fell 8.5% to $88.91, close to its $83 IPO price. New listings swing hard; wait for a few quarters of results.",
"<b>Plan for higher loan rates.</b> Bond yields fell, but Fed officials keep pushing for hikes. Lock fixed rates where you can and avoid new variable-rate debt.",
"<b>Gold is a hedge, not a rescue.</b> It fell to ~$3,540, the lowest since September 2025, as investors sold it to raise cash. Keep only a small slice for protection.",
"<b>Keep crypto small.</b> Bitcoin broke below $60,000 and is less than 2% above its summer low; only invest what you can afford to see fall a lot more.",
"<b>Thai investors: stay defensive.</b> The SET fell 1.31% to 1,453.28 and foreigners sold ฿2.4B; brokers see support at 1,435-1,400. Favour steady dividend payers and avoid using margin.",
"<b>Fuel keeps getting cheaper.</b> US diesel is ~$5.90 and oil had a third weekly loss, though Iran and Hormuz headlines can still cause spikes. Budget for swings."]};
// Glossary: m = regex matched against an element's text (li/td/h2); d = plain explanation + what it means now.
DASH.glossary={
fg:{m:"Fear & Greed",d:"CNN's 0-100 mood gauge for US stocks, built from 7 signals. 10 (9.7) = deep Extreme Fear, down from 19 Thursday, 37 a week ago and 29 a month ago. Six of the seven signals read extreme fear; only price strength reads fear."},
fgbands:{d:"0-25 Extreme Fear, 26-45 Fear, 46-55 Neutral, 56-75 Greed, 76-100 Extreme Greed. Fear often comes before rebounds, but not always."},
nk:{m:"Nuclear Escalation",d:"Our editorial 0-100 tension score from weighted news factors. Not a probability. ~50.7 = Elevated (up from 49.0): Russia hit Kyiv's bridges, a Houthi missile struck Riyadh, a tanker was hit near Hormuz, and the Trump-Xi-Putin declaration set no arms-control talks."},
nkbands:{d:"0-20 Low, 21-40 Guarded, 41-60 Elevated, 61-80 High, 81-100 Severe. Each factor's score × weight adds up to the total."},
mom:{m:"Market momentum",d:"S&P 500 vs its 125-day average. 0.2 = extreme fear, down from 1.2 as the S&P fell 3.7% into a correction."},
str:{m:"price strength",d:"Stocks at 52-week highs vs lows. 27.2 = fear, down from 31.2; NYSE had 565 new lows vs 14 highs."},
brd:{m:"breadth",d:"Volume in rising vs falling stocks. 20.0 = extreme fear, down from 30.8 as selling spread across the market."},
pc:{m:"Put/Call",d:"Compares bets on stocks falling vs rising. 2.0 = extreme fear, from 7.2: traders are piling into downside protection."},
vix:{m:"VIX",d:"The market's 'fear gauge' of expected S&P swings. 1.3 on CNN's 0-100 scale = extreme fear, as the VIX closed near 36, its highest since April 2025."},
sh:{m:"Safe-haven",d:"Stock returns vs bonds lately. 0.8 = extreme fear, from 9.0; bonds rallied hard while stocks fell 3.7%."},
jb:{m:"Junk bond",d:"Extra yield on risky company debt. 16.2 = extreme fear, down from 38.6 as investors shunned junk bonds."},
f1:{m:"Active wars",d:"Wars that could pull in nuclear powers. Scored 70 (unchanged): Trump says he may wait until 2027, but sources say a new US-Israeli assault on Iran is being weighed."},
f2:{m:"Russia-Ukraine",d:"A nuclear power at war. Scored 45 (from 42): Russia struck Kyiv's bridges and energy sites, killing at least 8, in retaliation for the Crimea bridge attack."},
f3:{m:"spillover",d:"Risk the Mideast war widens. Scored 91 (from 90): a Houthi missile hit Riyadh's PIF tower and a tanker caught fire after being hit near Hormuz."},
f4:{m:"diplomacy channels",d:"Are big powers talking? Higher = fewer working channels. Scored 10 (from 8): Trump praises Xi and Putin, but the summit declaration left out Ukraine and Iran."},
f5:{m:"Arms-control",d:"Nuclear threats and treaty news. Scored 30 (from 28): the declaration sets no arms-control talks and Trump says it is 'hard' to give up nuclear weapons."},
sp:{m:"S&P",d:"500 big US companies, the main US stock benchmark. ~6,910 Friday (−3.70%), a seventh straight loss; now in a correction, 10%+ below its 6 Oct record."},
dow:{m:"Dow",d:"30 large 'blue-chip' US stocks, more old-economy. −1.93% Friday (−950 pts) to about 48,147, also in a correction; −8% this week."},
ndq:{m:"Nasdaq",d:"Tech-heavy US index. −5.28% Friday to about 22,618, now down 2.7% for 2026 after its worst week since March 2020."},
y10:{m:"10Y",d:"Yield on 10-year US government bonds, which drives loan rates. ~4.91% Friday, down ~14bp and back below 5% as investors fled to safety."},
wti:{m:"WTI",d:"US crude oil price. ~$84.0 (+0.9%) Friday as December WTI expired at $83.98, but −5.2% for the week."},
brent:{m:"Brent",d:"Global benchmark crude. ~$92.6 at Friday's settle (+0.64%), −3.4% this week and −21% over three weeks."},
dsl:{m:"diesel",d:"US average diesel price. ~$5.90/gal (AAA, 20 Nov), down from $6.06 a week ago."},
gold:{m:"^Gold$|Gold and|gold slice",d:"Classic safe haven. ~$3,540 spot (−2.4%), the lowest since September 2025, as investors sold it to raise cash."},
btc:{m:"Bitcoin|BTC",d:"The largest crypto. ~$58.9k = bearish: below $60,000 for the first time since July with $1.5B of liquidations; it trades with tech, not as a haven."},
bull:{d:"BULLISH = we expect it to rise or hold strong. MILDLY = a leaning, not a strong view."},
neu:{d:"NEUTRAL = no clear direction; it could go either way."},
bear:{d:"BEARISH = we expect it to fall or stay weak."},
ff:{m:"Fed funds",d:"The Fed's key short-term interest rate. 3.75-4.00% after September's hike, held 28 Oct; a December hike is ~92% priced for 8-9 Dec."},
cpi:{m:"CPI",d:"Consumer price inflation. October rose 0.4% MoM (est. 0.3%) and core 0.3% (est. 0.2%), a third straight upside surprise; no official YoY because of last year's data gap, well above the Fed's 2% goal."},
ppi:{m:"PPI",d:"Prices businesses pay, an early inflation signal. October rose 0.3% MoM (est. 0.4%) and 6.5% YoY, the highest since November 2022; core +0.3%."},
odds:{m:"Hike odds|Fed odds",d:"Market-implied chance of a Fed hike (fed funds futures, CME FedWatch). ~92% for a quarter point in December, down from ~100% Thursday."},
dxy:{m:"Dollar index",d:"DXY: the dollar against 6 major currencies. ~103.8 Friday, little changed and just under its recent 19-month high."},
jpy:{m:"USD/JPY|Yen",d:"Yen per dollar. ~158.5 after the yen firmed as a haven, still near the 160 level where Japan has warned about intervention."},
cds:{m:"CDS",d:"Credit default swap: insurance against a company defaulting. CoreWeave's CDS went past 11% (a distress level) in October; its bonds now yield ~15% (CNBC, 17 Nov)."},
bot:{m:"BOT policy|BoT meeting|BOT MPC|BoT decision|BoT held|BoT kept",d:"Bank of Thailand's key rate. Held at 1.00% on 28 Oct; Governor Witai says the BoT aims to keep rates steady to support growth but is data-dependent; 2026 GDP forecast kept at 2.4%; next decision 23 Dec."},
set:{m:"SET",d:"SET = Thai stock index; SET50 = its 50 biggest stocks. 1,453.28 Fri 20 Nov (−1.31%), low 1,443; KS sees support at 1,435 and 1,410."},
flow:{m:"Foreign flows|foreigners",d:"Net buying minus selling by foreign investors. −฿2,366M of Thai stocks on Fri 20 Nov, after −฿2,495M Thursday; −฿6,155M so far in November."},
dca:{m:"DCA",d:"Dollar-cost averaging: invest a fixed amount on a schedule regardless of price, which smooths out bad timing."}};

